   "author": "Hollowmere team (agent X)",
   "story": "In the first week of the quarantine the Cordon flew its medical team out of the valley: Dr. Ama Osei, two nurses, a medic, the flight medic Lt. Ingrid Vos and a case of Bloom samples on cold chain, under a two-man escort, in a twin-engine transport with Capt. Teo Reyes at the controls. Twelve minutes out the Hum came up through the airframe like a bad engine and both engines lost power together. Reyes put her into the timber. The fuselage broke behind the wing: the forward section went on and buried its nose in the bank; the tail stayed fifteen metres back among the trunks it had snapped. Nobody came. The survivors made a camp in the cargo hold and waited for the rescue the radio kept promising. Osei treated the injured, then the feverish, then each other. The pilots stayed on the flight deck with the radio. Vos carried the sample case into the tail's equipment bay, deadbolted the hatch, and sent the key forward to the captain so nobody could make her open it.",
